# {{NAME}} website

Built with the [Zagware website framework](https://github.com/{{FRAMEWORK_REPO}}). All content lives in `site.config.mjs`; images go in `assets/img/`.

| | URL |
|---|---|
| Preview (GitHub Pages, noindex) | {{PAGES_URL}} |
| Production (Cloudflare) | {{PRODUCTION_URL}} |

## Develop

```bash
npm install
npx zsite dev .          # http://localhost:4173, live reload
npx zsite components     # list available section types
npx zsite check .        # build every target; fails on warnings or broken links
```

## Preview (POC)

Pushing to `main` runs **Preview (GitHub Pages)**. One-time setup: repo Settings → Pages → Source: **GitHub Actions**.

## Go live on Cloudflare

1. Put the domain's zone on the Zagware Cloudflare account. Copy the mail records (MX/SPF/DKIM/DMARC) before switching nameservers.
2. In `wrangler.jsonc`, uncomment `routes`. If the site has a Worker (`worker.mjs`), also run `npx wrangler d1 create {{SLUG}}-site`, paste the id into `wrangler.jsonc`, and add the secrets listed at the top of that file.
3. Add the repo secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`.
4. `git tag v1.0.0 && git push --tags`. This runs **Deploy (Cloudflare)**: build, D1 migrations, deploy, smoke test.

## Framework updates

```bash
npm install github:zagware/website-framework#vX.Y.Z && npx zsite check .
```

Only upgrade to versions that have been verified on the devtest site.
